/A 42 0 R
/Alt (Cross-sectional diagram of a reactor illustrating labeled layers. The outermost layer is "Blanket salt," followed by a layer of "Outer heavy water." The central region contains "Fuel salt," surrounded by "Inner heavy water." The design shows the containment structure.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 28 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
16 0 obj
<<
/A 42 0 R
/Alt (Cross-sectional schematic of a nuclear reactor featuring multiple circular layers. The labeled sections include blanket salt, outer heavy water, fuel salt, and inner heavy water, shown in alternating black and red lines.)
/K 1
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 28 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
17 0 obj
<<
/A 42 0 R
/Alt (Three bar graphs compare relative differences in various isotopes for three models. Graph \(a\) shows fuel salt isotopes; graph \(b\) displays blanket salt isotopes; graph \(c\) features OGS isotopes. Blue bars compare OpenMC with Serpent, and red bars compare OpenMC with EQLOD. Graph \(c\) has a significant red bar at 13.59 percent. Each graph highlights isotopic differences, with varying magnitudes for different isotopes.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 34 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
18 0 obj
<<
/A 42 0 R
/Alt (Three bar charts labeled \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) compare relative differences in percent across various isotopes. Each chart has two color-coded comparisons: OpenMC versus Serpent in blue, and OpenMC versus EQLOD in red. Chart \(a\) focuses on "Fuel salt," chart \(b\) on "Blanket salt," and chart \(c\) on "OGS," displaying differences for isotopes such as uranium and cesium. Data points vary, with notable differences in chart \(c\) highlighted by a red bar labeled 13.53 percent. The x-axis shows relative difference percentages ranging from -1.00 to 1.00.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 37 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
19 0 obj
<<
/A 42 0 R
/Alt (Three bar charts display the relative differences in isotopes for Model 3 across different salts. \(a\) Fuel salt shows bars with values around zero. \(b\) Blanket salt features wider variations, including a prominent positive difference for barium-139. \(c\) OGS indicates outliers for xenon-133 and krypton-85, with other differences near zero. All charts use green bars for "OpenMC vs EQLO 0D" comparisons, with isotopes labeled on the vertical axes and relative difference percentages on the horizontal.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 39 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
